{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/general-onyx-path-discussion/1533360-strange-call-to-an-old-freelancer","id":1533360,"title":"Strange Call to an Old Freelancer","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","General Onyx Path Discussion"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-03-29T09:44:16-07:00","id":1533360,"title":"Strange Call to an Old Freelancer","content":"This morning I received an odd phone call from a woman who called herself &quot;Maggie,&quot; who claimed to represent a company called, I think, &quot;Lion Leaf Publishing&quot;, or maybe it was &quot;Promotions&quot; -- it all happened pretty fast. Alse, her Asian accent means I'm not entirely sure she said, &quot;Lion Leaf.&quot; Anyway, she asked if I was the Dean Shomshak who'd written <i>Vampire,&quot; </i>which their company had picked as to promote, and would I be interested in participating?<br /> <br /> This happens to me about once a year. Morning phone call from someone in Asia who wants to promote something I worked on for White Wolf. I always point out that this was work made for hire, I do not own the work in question, and the intellectual property rights passed to Onyx Path. Apparently people in China or wherever are not good at reading indicia and tracking corporate changes -- or it's just a scam, hoping I'll pay them for nonexistent promotions. I suspect the latter, but I do wonder if Onyx Path has ever been contacted by Asian companies wanting to republish or promote the old White Wolf books. Or, for that matter, if other old freelancers receive such calls.<br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-29T21:24:22-07:00","id":1533370,"title":"","content":"Wait, wouldn\u2019t the property rights to old WW books be Paradox\u2019s property now, not OPP?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-30T18:28:11-07:00","id":1533400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/general-onyx-path-discussion/1533360-strange-call-to-an-old-freelancer?p=1533370#post1533370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, wouldn\u2019t the property rights to old WW books be Paradox\u2019s property now, not OPP?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yes, but considering the caller was reaching out to someone who last freelanced for WW before OPP (according to the WW wiki) existed there are a number of reasons they might reach out to OPP instead of Paradox.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>They are scammers who are targeting people who wrote for Vampire in the past and intentionally avoiding people currently associated with the IP who can in theory easily verify the legitimacy of the claim</li> <li>They don\u2019t know Paradox is the current IP holder, which has come up several times. For example a number of people on Twitter got made at OPP over art issues with W5 because they didn\u2019t know OPP wasn\u2019t involved with it.</li> <li>By choice or lack of access (I can\u2019t speak to Modiphus but Renegade has been known to have issues with distribution outside of the US), whatever Lion Leaf is promoting is dealing with legacy material and is either not interested in talking to people involved with V5.</li> </ol>All of the above are reasons they might reach out to people connected with OPP as there are a handful of folks still around who were there in the WW days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}